}⁡(3z)\\,k.\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z).$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186351365 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e91b9e21-1500-52f9-9378-332978dc9aa7" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186351365 #edb/ref 1074 "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{i}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,\\text{j}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,\\text{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y{e}^{xy},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{xy}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =x{e}^{xy} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(z) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z) \\\\ h(z) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3z)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3z)+C.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186351371 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186351019 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186351371 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81752" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186351371 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186351371 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=(yz{e}^{xz}+z)\\,i+({e}^{xz}+1)\\,j+(xy{e}^{xz}+x)\\,k.\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z).$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186351371 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dfdbf33d-2f2f-5cc3-b43d-2537f87d3a7e" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186351371 #edb/ref 1074 "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{i}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,\\text{j}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,\\text{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=yz{e}^{xz}+z,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{xz}+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{xz}+x\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (yz{e}^{xz}+z)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =y{e}^{xz}+xz+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{xz}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{xz}+1$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{xz}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & ={e}^{xz}+1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =y+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=y+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xz}+xz+y+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{xz}+x+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{xz}+x$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy{e}^{xz}+x+{h}^{′}(z) & =zy{e}^{xz}+x \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xz}+xz+y+C.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406691 #edb/ref 1081 "f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406691 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406691 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "03292879-7e19-58c5-bf30-9a82b7757e44" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406692 #edb/ref 1081 "f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy+C" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406692 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406692 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "03fb1154-e9d5-5abf-a426-4de833dd30db" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406693 #edb/ref 1081 "f(x,y)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+{y}^{3}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406693 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406693 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "0dea30ea-6d79-5529-9cdd-2d23960e3a15" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406694 #edb/ref 1081 "f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+C" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406694 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406694 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "10ef096b-3da6-5469-9aaf-056abb9c9b31" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406695 #edb/ref 1081 "f(x,y)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+3y+C" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406695 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406695 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "1bfaa94c-d375-5358-a83c-08ec5ee1ffba" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406696 #edb/ref 1081 "f(x,y)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+2y+C" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406696 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406696 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "1e611253-3d99-509d-a228-1da84f8f823e" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406697 #edb/r